# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Obsidian runtime state that must NOT be published.
#
# The vault ships a *minimal* .obsidian so that cloning it and opening it in
# Obsidian Just Works. Everything listed here is per-machine personal state.
#
# Deliberately NOT using a blanket `plugins/*/data.json` ignore: the Excalidraw
# plugin's data.json IS committed (it wires MindMap Builder into the sidepanel),
# and git's negation rules do not behave predictably for files inside an ignored
# directory. Listing the unwanted files explicitly avoids that trap entirely.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/workspaces.json
.obsidian/hotkeys.json
.obsidian/graph.json
.obsidian/backlink.json
.obsidian/canvas.json
.obsidian/page-preview.json
.obsidian/types.json
.obsidian/webviewer.json
.obsidian/core-plugins-migration.json
.obsidian/appearance.json
.obsidian/community-plugins.json.bak

# Credentials live in plugin data files (the AI plugins store plaintext API
# keys). If you add any plugin beyond Excalidraw, ignore its data.json here.
.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-copilot/data.json
.obsidian/plugins/copilot/data.json
.obsidian/plugins/remotely-save/data.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site build artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local scratch
*.bak
.bak/
